note: batch 10n2, part A: a field order change under a derive of the proc macro crate `depot` whose code does not read the fields; with the build check, the expansion records show the same code in the two trees, so the order change needs no reason (the fact has a note); with no build check, the case `names/order_third_party` keeps the spotlight
rule+: R65.9-1
must_match: member order of `shop::Item`: `a, b` → `b, a`
must_match: the member order needs no reason: each macro of the type \(`Marker`\) makes the same code in the two versions
must_not_match: spotlight
